{
  "title": "arc-principle-validation: the code, data, results and papers of the ARC Theory research programme",
  "upload_type": "software",
  "language": "eng",
  "description": "The public repository of Michael Darius Eastwood's research programme in Recursive Dynamics, the field he founded, and its ARC Theory of recursive self-improvement: the theory's five laws, each a law under test, the studies registered to test them, and the programme's engineering and governance papers. It holds 35 of the programme's 36 documents (all but its Priority Index, which is held on OSF), each in its own folder under papers/ at its latest version, and the code, data and results of the programme's experiments, published as they stand. Each document's canonical record, with every version, is on OSF, and each document's DOI is listed under related works (the working report, which has no DOI, by its OSF address). This record archives the repository as a whole at one date, so that the code and data behind a reported result can be cited and checked. Licences: the code, experiments, scripts, data and results are licensed under the Apache License 2.0, and the papers, text and figures under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENCE, NOTICE, LICENCE-CODE.md and LICENCE-PAPERS.md).",
